                                                                                     "value":  "={{ $json.repeat_blocked === true ? \u0027The same confirmation card for the sync_plan action was already not confirmed in this turn, no new card was sent. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. Answer the user now, based on the earlier result.\u0027 : $json.reason === \u0027owner_only\u0027 ? \u0027Only the household owner may do the sync_plan action; no card was sent. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. Tell the user only the owner can do this.\u0027 : ({ declined: \u0027The user tapped the cancel button on the confirmation card for the sync_plan action. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. This was their decision, not an error: say it was cancelled and ask what to change, if anything.\u0027, expired: \u0027The confirmation card for the sync_plan action expired: nobody tapped a button within the time limit, so nobody declined it. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. Tell the user the card ran out of time, not that they cancelled it, and ask whether to send it again.\u0027, owner_declined: \u0027The household owner declined the confirmation card for the sync_plan action after the user had confirmed it. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. Tell the user the owner declined it; the user did not cancel it.\u0027, owner_expired: \u0027The household owner did not answer the confirmation card for the sync_plan action within the time limit; the user had already confirmed it. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. Tell the user the owner did not answer in time and ask whether to send it again.\u0027 })[$json.outcome] || \u0027The confirmation card for the sync_plan action was not confirmed. Nothing was saved. Do NOT call this tool again in this turn. Tell the user it was not confirmed and ask whether to try again or what to change.\u0027 }}",
